{"name":"Purple Cheeks","hex":"#b67ca2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"cheeks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cheek","Ass; sex."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cheek"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheeks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheek","blocks":[{"text":"The cheeks constitute the area of the face below the eyes and between the nose and the left or right ear. Buccal means relating to the cheek. In humans, the region is innervated by the buccal nerve. The area between the inside of the cheek and the teeth and gums is called the vestibule or buccal pouch or buccal cavity and forms part of the mouth. In other animals, the cheeks may also be referred to as \"jowls\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Cheek.jpg/330px-Cheek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheek"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/1280px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/500px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/1280px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/500px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An eastern chipmunk using its buccal pouch to store food","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/G